diff --git a/docs/api/aurora-water.md b/docs/api/aurora-water.md
index fd951b8..6fb30e2 100644
--- a/docs/api/aurora-water.md
+++ b/docs/api/aurora-water.md
@@ -56,3 +56,35 @@ resize. It reports an explicit skip when no GPU is available; that is not GPU
 validation. Test the actual game with both sky/material stages (their group 3
 layouts differ), material-only/TAA, hot reload, resize and a previous API pack.
 Use disposable homes/worlds as required by AGENTS.md.
+
+## water.3: continuous immersion and a pack-owned water environment
+
+`0.1-aurora-water.3` inherits the scene snapshot contract. Every stage appends
+one aligned vector to Frame: `water: vec4<f32>`. `water.x` is continuous camera
+water coverage in 0..1; `water.y` is 1 when the custom environment is enabled,
+otherwise 0; z/w are reserved zeros. Legacy Frame field offsets and its WGSL
+size stay unchanged for older API lines. The renderer allocates 16 trailing
+bytes, with a layout test checking the extended prefix and offset.
+
+The game measures the fraction of a 0.36-block cube around the interpolated
+camera occupied by water cells, then applies smoothstep. It uses the existing
+camera fluid-height rule, including flowing/waterlogged fluid. Adjacent cells
+sum without artificial seams. This is a visual coverage approximation, not
+physical eye submersion or a resolved near-plane waterline. It has no temporal
+history: teleports do not retain the previous water state.
+
+The API requires at least one post stage. Only a successfully compiled/running
+water.3 pack enables the replacement. In the Overworld, without blindness,
+darkness, night vision, lava or powder snow, native atmospheric/distance fog is
+retained and native water fog is not baked into the scene. The pack MUST compose
+its water attenuation in post using the depth and continuous coverage. The
+stock binary water screen overlay is disabled; world/hand FOV fluid scaling is
+interpolated using the same coverage and the user's FOV Effects scale. Physical
+fluid detection, player swimming, breathing, audio and ticks are unchanged.
+
+Switching to a previous API or no pack restores native fog/FOV/overlay. Other
+dimensions and the listed statuses retain the native environment (`water.y=0`),
+so the pack must return its unmodified post input there. This API does not expose
+per-pixel water exit depth; a screen-space water pass still approximates mixed
+water/air paths and transparent layers. The first-person hand and HUD are drawn
+after the world's post chain and are not colour-graded by this water pass.
